**Mechanism confirmed:**
- Pings from `host_1_1_1_1` (10.1.1.2) and `host_2_1_1_1` (10.2.1.2) arrive at `web_server_1` via the OSPF-routed path through the core.
- `web_server_1` needs to route the ICMP reply (and TCP SYN-ACK for HTTP) back to 10.1.x.x / 10.2.x.x via the gateway (10.200.0.1).
- Without a default route, the kernel returns "Network is unreachable" and drops the reply — the host sees a timeout.
- Same-farm hosts (10.200.0.x subnet) communicate via L2/ARP directly — no gateway needed — so those pings succeed.

